.TH mkdir 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
mkdir \- create directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkdir
[\fB\-p\fR] \fIdirectory ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkdir
creates each
.IR directory .
The mode is 0777 less the current
.BR umask .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
Create any missing intermediate directories on the path, and do not
treat an already existing directory as an error \- including the final
one.
.PP
.B \-p
is only recognised as the
.I first
argument.
.SH NOTES
There is no
.B \-m
option; set the mode afterwards with
.BR chmod (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (1),
.BR chmod (1)
